WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.200
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar!

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.080
In the following star shaped figure,

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.460
what is the measure of angle A in degrees?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.980
This problem appeared on a test given to eighth grade students in 1999.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.440
Approximately 75% of students did not mark the correct answer.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.060
Can you figure it out?

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.080
Give this problem a try, and when your ready keep watching the video for the solution.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.920
One way to solve this problem is by using several geometric principles.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.440
One principle is that a straight line measures 180 degrees.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.340
We can look at the angle next to 100 degrees,

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:52.960
and calculate that  it must be 180 minus 100 or 80 degrees.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:01:00.340
Similarly, the angle next to 110 degrees must equal 180 minus 110,

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.600
and therefore that angle is equal to 70 degrees.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:10.380
We now use the principle, that the angles in a triangle sum up to 180 degrees.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:18.920
In the triangle with 40 degrees and 70 degrees, the final angle will be equal to 180 minus 40 minus 70.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.560
So the final angle of this triangle is 70 degrees.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.600
We then use the principle, that vertical angles have equal measure,

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.020
so the angle above 70 degrees is equal to 70 degrees,

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:39.360
and finally we can use the principle that the three angles in a triangle sum to 180 degrees.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:45.340
This means angle A is equal to 180 minus 80 minus 70.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.080
And therefore angle A is equal to 30 degrees.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.540
So that's our answer: 30 degrees.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.640
There is in fact a quicker way to solve this problem.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.680
You only need to use one principle,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.620
which is that the angles in a triangle sum up to 180 degrees.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.000
The trick is to look at the correct triangles.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.600
First we'll consider the triangle that involves a 40-degree angle and a 100-degree angle.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.940
We know that all three angles add up to 180 degrees.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:26.800
The third angle therefore will be 180 minus 100 minus 40.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.480
This angle is equal to 40 degrees.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.560
We now consider another triangle, which involves angle A.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.740
The other angles are 110 and 40 degrees.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:46.980
Therefore angle A will equal 180 minus 110 minus 40.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.300
So we directly get that angle A equals 30 degrees.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.840
And we get to our answer much quicker.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.060
Did you figure out this problem?

